<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigismund of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 524</span> · Also known as Saint Sigismund</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigismund of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> from 516 to 524. A convert from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a> to Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, he founded the abbey of Saint-Maurice d'Agaune. Defeated by the Frankish kings, he was captured and put to death with his family on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer of Orléans</a> in 524, and was later venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigismund-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Sigismund of Burgundy" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Jansoone (JoJan) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Sigismund.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
